Labeled row written to `coder-3.json`: AB 2655 (2023-2024), which Berman authored and was signed into law, coded as `chair-shaped` for rung 1 (legally require platforms to remove false information) — his own-act, in-term record, with the removal mandate as the operative clause and the labeling provision treated as a supplementary duty for a separate content category rather than a label-instead-of-removal position.
